  "central_assessment": {
    "confidence_assessment": "High confidence on quantitative modeling and valuation math (regression tests pass). Qualitative claims strictly audited: console installed count (>30,000) downgraded to industry estimate; consumables gross margin (>75%) downgraded to unaudited management assertion; non-equipment revenue share (88.4%) certified from audited Form 20-F financial statements.",
    "disposition": "WATCH_CONDITIONS",
    "disposition_label": "Watch \u2014 Conditions Required for Entry",
    "main_uncertainty": "Commercial transition velocity to the next-generation Unity surgical console platform, competitive intraocular lens pricing in EMEA/APAC tenders, and future Swiss AGM approval timing for additional capital return authorizations.",
    "presentation_summary": "Alcon Inc. is the global market leader in ophthalmology, holding the #1 position in Surgical and #2 in Vision Care. The company operates an exceptional razor-and-blade business model characterized by proprietary surgical consoles (Centurion, Constellation, LuxOR) driving high-margin single-use consumables, cassettes, and intraocular lenses (IOLs). Audited FY2025 Form 20-F disclosures confirm that 88.4% of total net sales ($9,119M of $10,319M) represent non-equipment repeat procedural and consumer replenishment demand (NOT contracted subscription revenue). However, at the frozen October 21, 2026 reference price of $67.43 USD, the market embeds a 6.51% 5-year revenue CAGR at 20.5% operating margin. Under certified Base DCF assumptions with scenario-derived net debt (6.5% CAGR, 18.5% EBIT margin, WACC 7.25%, g 2.50%), the expected 5-year discrete annual IRR is 7.64% (7.65% calendar XIRR). This approaches but remains just below the institutional cost of equity (7.80%) and 8.00% capital hurdle. Retained strictly on watch: entry requires market pullbacks toward the accumulation ceiling of $66.31 (8.0% hurdle) or $64.82 (8.5% hurdle).",
    "price_watch_condition": "Accumulate only on pullbacks below $66.31 for an 8.0% expected return, or below $64.82 for an 8.5% return ($60.56 for 10.0% hurdle). At current $67.43 reference price, risk/reward remains uncompensated.",
    "strongest_opposing_evidence": "Expected 5-year IRR of 7.64% remains below institutional cost of equity (7.80%) and provides thin equity risk premium over US 10-year Treasuries (4.10%); significant capital expenditures required for contact lens and intraocular lens manufacturing expansion; approved buyback capacity ($1,200M active) requires future AGM renewals beyond May 2029 to finance modeled $1,800M share repurchases.",
    "strongest_supporting_evidence": "88.37% non-equipment sales share ($9,119M / $10,319M in FY2025 audited Form 20-F); high surgical console installed base switching friction; global ophthalmic surgical duopoly with steady procedural growth driven by aging global demographics.",
    "summary_provenance": "DERIVED_SYNTHESIS"
  },
